{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"2e98efbe33829382","name":"card_unit_kokuras_sword","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Japan/BrothersInArms/units/card_unit_kokuras_sword","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"KOKURA'S SWORD","text":"Destruction: If it's the enemy turn, add a random Japanese ground unit to your support line and give it this ability.","flavorText":"The 12th Division of the Imperial Japanese Army was an infantry division that saw action during WWII. It played a role in various military campaigns, particularly in China during the Second Sino-Japanese War. Its code name was the Sword Division and it recruited primarily from the northern part of the island of Kyūshū. Its original headquarters were located in the Kokura castle, in the city of Kitakyushu. In 1940, the 12th Division underwent reorganization, becoming a triangular division with the transfer of its IJA 14th Infantry Regiment to the IJA 25th Division. Under the command of Lieutenant General Masakazu Kawabe, the division was permanently stationed in Manchukuo (now Manchuria) from July 1940, falling under the jurisdiction of the Japanese Third Army in Dongning. Its main tasks involved policing and anti-partisan operations. As the Pacific War took a turn for the worse for Japan in 1944, the 12th Division was relocated to Hsinchu, Taiwan, to reinforce the defenses of the 10th Area Army. Eventually, it became part of the 40th Army when it was stationed in Taiwan in early 1945. However, since the Allies bypassed Taiwan and landed on Okinawa instead, the 12th Division spent the remainder of World War II as a garrison force in Taiwan, without engaging in combat.","faction":"Japan","type":"infantry","rarity":"Unique","cost":5,"operationCost":2,"attack":6,"defense":6},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_kokuras_sword","title":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_unit_kokuras_sword_title","SourceString":"KOKURA'S SWORD","LocalizedString":"KOKURA'S SWORD"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":6,"defense":6,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Japan","kredits":5,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_unit_kokuras_sword_text","SourceString":"Destruction: If it's the enemy turn, add a random Japanese ground unit to your support line and give it this ability.","LocalizedString":"Destruction: If it's the enemy turn, add a random Japanese ground unit to your support line and give it this ability."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_unit_kokuras_sword_history","SourceString":"The 12th Division of the Imperial Japanese Army was an infantry division that saw action during WWII. It played a role in various military campaigns, particularly in China during the Second Sino-Japanese War. Its code name was the Sword Division and it recruited primarily from the northern part of the island of Kyūshū. Its original headquarters were located in the Kokura castle, in the city of Kitakyushu. In 1940, the 12th Division underwent reorganization, becoming a triangular division with the transfer of its IJA 14th Infantry Regiment to the IJA 25th Division. Under the command of Lieutenant General Masakazu Kawabe, the division was permanently stationed in Manchukuo (now Manchuria) from July 1940, falling under the jurisdiction of the Japanese Third Army in Dongning. Its main tasks involved policing and anti-partisan operations. As the Pacific War took a turn for the worse for Japan in 1944, the 12th Division was relocated to Hsinchu, Taiwan, to reinforce the defenses of the 10th Area Army. Eventually, it became part of the 40th Army when it was stationed in Taiwan in early 1945. However, since the Allies bypassed Taiwan and landed on Okinawa instead, the 12th Division spent the remainder of World War II as a garrison force in Taiwan, without engaging in combat.","LocalizedString":"The 12th Division of the Imperial Japanese Army was an infantry division that saw action during WWII. It played a role in various military campaigns, particularly in China during the Second Sino-Japanese War. Its code name was the Sword Division and it recruited primarily from the northern part of the island of Kyūshū. Its original headquarters were located in the Kokura castle, in the city of Kitakyushu. In 1940, the 12th Division underwent reorganization, becoming a triangular division with the transfer of its IJA 14th Infantry Regiment to the IJA 25th Division. Under the command of Lieutenant General Masakazu Kawabe, the division was permanently stationed in Manchukuo (now Manchuria) from July 1940, falling under the jurisdiction of the Japanese Third Army in Dongning. Its main tasks involved policing and anti-partisan operations. As the Pacific War took a turn for the worse for Japan in 1944, the 12th Division was relocated to Hsinchu, Taiwan, to reinforce the defenses of the 10th Area Army. Eventually, it became part of the 40th Army when it was stationed in Taiwan in early 1945. However, since the Allies bypassed Taiwan and landed on Okinawa instead, the 12th Division spent the remainder of World War II as a garrison force in Taiwan, without engaging in combat."},"operationCost":2,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Unique","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::BrothersInArms","isReserved":true,"usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardDestroyed","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnEndOfTurn","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardReset","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardSuppressed"],"extraHelpTextBubbleTypes":["EHelpBubbleTypes::Destruction"],"draftBaseWeight":0.8,"hasDestruction":true,"soundBlowUp":{"ObjectName":"SoundCue'au_inf_conrete'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Explosions_SFX/Cues/au_inf_conrete.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Japan/Spring2023Candidates/t_m_sword.t_m_sword","SubPathString":""},"artist":"Volmi Games","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/KOKURA_S_SWORD.KOKURA_S_SWORD","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":707.0,"Y":731.0},"historyPhotoDescriptio